<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-ICI Australia net falls 26.7 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-ICI Australia net falls 26.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>		  (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    350.1 vs 408.1</p>
<p>    Net profit			    197.1 vs 268.8</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     26.0 vs 32.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Chemicals group ICI Australia Ltd is 62.4 percent owned by Imperial Chemical Industries Plc.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)		 44 vs 52</p>
<p>    Sales (billion)			3.46 vs 3.37</p>
<p>    Other income			   50.0 vs 45.2</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		  loss 23.1 vs nil</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    66.5 vs 90.7</p>
<p>Pay date Jan 24</p>
<p>Reg date Jan 10</p>
<p>    Tax				     108.8 vs 124.2</p>
<p>    Interest				 31.2 vs 21.2</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  123.9 vs 132.1</p>
<p>    Minorities			     21.2 vs 15.1</p>
<p>NOTE: ICI Australia said the abnormal loss reflected restructuring costs. It said 11 cents of the final dividend of 26 cents a share is fully franked.</p>
<p>Divisional trading profit before abnormal items.</p>
<p>    Fertilizers and crop care	    77 vs  32</p>
<p>    Chemicals				  96 vs 113</p>
<p>    Mining services			  88 vs  80</p>
<p>    Plastics				    2 vs  73</p>
<p>    Consumer products			65 vs  85</p>
<p>    Advanced sciences			44 vs  37</p>
<p>    Total				     372 vs 420</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
